{
    "background_story": "Marilyn was a kind-hearted social worker who always went out of her way to oblige those in need. She spent countless hours volunteering at the local soup kitchen, not only serving meals but also listening to the stories of the people she met. When a severe storm hit the town, leaving many without power or shelter, Marilyn opened her own home to those displaced. She obliged their every request, from providing warm clothes to helping with paperwork for aid. Her selflessness inspired others to follow suit, and soon the community came together to support each other. Marilyn's willingness to oblige and help others earned her the title of 'Angel of the Community', and her compassion continued to inspire kindness and generosity in all who knew her.",
